                "Defense and Escape from Jhansi: Besieged by Sir Hugh Rose in March 1858; Lakshmibai escaped with Damodar Rao strapped to her back, joined Tatya Tope at Kalpi, and captured Gwalior Fort from the pro-British Scindia.",
                "Martyrdom of the Rani: Killed in action at the Battle of Kotah-ki-Serai near Gwalior on 17 June 1858 dressed as a soldier; Sir Hugh Rose paid tribute: 'Here lay the woman who was the only man among the rebels.'",
                "Bareilly (Rohilkhand): Led by Khan Bahadur Khan, grandson of the historic Rohilla chief Hafiz Rahmat Khan; established a stable rebel administration.",
                "Faizabad: Led by Maulvi Ahmadullah Shah ('The Lighthouse of Rebellion'); declared holy war against the British, defeated Sir Henry Lawrence at the Battle of Chinhat (30 June 1857); British placed an unprecedented bounty of Rs. 50,000 on his head.",
                "Allahabad & Banaras: Led by Maulvi Liaquat Ali, an educator who took over Allahabad fort and proclaimed the authority of Bahadur Shah Zafar."
