                "Intelligentsia Support: Harish Chandra Mukherjee, editor of 'The Hindu Patriot', championed the peasants' cause; Sisir Kumar Ghosh reported on the atrocities.",
                "Dinabandhu Mitra's 'Nil Darpan' (1860): A powerful Bengali play that realistically depicted the torture, rape, and terror inflicted by European planters.",
                "Michael Madhusudan Dutt translated 'Nil Darpan' into English; Reverend James Long published it and was sentenced to one month in prison by a British court.",
