                "Moplah (Mapilla) Rebellion (1921): In Malabar (Kerala); Muslim tenant cultivators (Moplahs) rose against oppressive Hindu Jenmis (landlords) and the British state; merged with the Khilafat and Non-Cooperation Movements; leaders included Ali Musaliyar and Variyankunnath Kunjahammed Haji; tragedy of the 'Wagon Tragedy' (67 Moplah prisoners suffocated in a closed freight train).",
                "Bardoli Satyagraha (1928): In Surat district, Gujarat; against a 22% (initially 30%) arbitrary land revenue hike by the Bombay government.",
